 is pointing in the *positive* $x$-direction, so the $i$ component of our vector field is positive. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=-2\\,i,\\,H(x,y,z)=-\\,i\n$$\n\n- Finally, we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $i$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y,z)=-{e}^{y}\\,k\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram doesn't correspond to any of the listed vector fields."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371665 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6291ddda-70de-5718-9bfc-105bebc04e63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371667} {:answer/id #uuid "9c909eaf-192d-5156-bfd4-507f1094667b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y,z)=i+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371668} {:answer/id #uuid "c96f1d9d-d0ba-5ae3-bcdf-556a56778e37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y,z)=-2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371669} {:answer/id #uuid "cef6452c-f105-5828-9426-ff34265362da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y,z)=3\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371670} {:answer/id #uuid "15bc72b2-4db5-5aa4-9cbf-0714e10fa1a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cef6452c-f105-5828-9426-ff34265362da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y,z)=3\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371670} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9373a90-9549-57f3-9c97-5391475a1938" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371666}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6439da6-7b28-559c-9b9e-cf7883c3a650" :question/math-academy-id "q-122662" :question/problem "![](images/8d/8d978a63c661ddb2adfca6f0be5315778abb2464a1e1f45f78dedfa4cbaa5d12.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- Each vector in our vector field is parallel to the $y$-axis. So, the $i$ and $k$ components of our vector field are zero everywhere. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nH(x,y,z)=i+k\n$$\n\n- Moreover, each vector in our vector field is pointing in the *positive* $y$-direction, so the $j$ component of our vector field is positive. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=-2\\,j\n$$\n\n- Finally, we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $j$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $G(x,y,z)=3\\,j.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a066e71c-60d5-5fbb-80e0-33c201104192" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375806} {:answer/id #uuid "251b33e0-026f-5d55-b464-0243c1951e03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y,z)=i-j-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375807} {:answer/id #uuid "f666e84d-6691-5a63-8975-137451851b83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y,z)=y\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375808} {:answer/id #uuid "e4e84d30-dd2a-5fa6-ae2d-25fd3bdb8810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y,z)=i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375809} {:answer/id #uuid "11bfffa1-bd3e-551d-accb-96f12bb32b33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y,z)=-i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11bfffa1-bd3e-551d-accb-96f12bb32b33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y,z)=-i" :